***************************************************************** 2825 1451
 New evaluation above the resonance region, below 20 MeV          2825 1451
                                        T. Kawano (LANL) Aug 2012 2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
   Many of sections in MF=3,4,6,12, and 14 were updated based on  2825 1451
the CoH3 calculations. We preserved the old document              2825 1451
in MF=1 by D.C. Larson, et al. of ENDF/B-VI for record keeping    2825 1451
purpose. Although the default claculations fit the                2825 1451
avaiable experimental data reasonably well, and give similar      2825 1451
cross sections in ENDF/B-VI, some modifications to the            2825 1451
excitation functions were made; (n,p), (n,2n), (n,alpha),         2825 1451
and (n,np) channels. The (n,2p) and (n,p alpha) cross sections    2825 1451
were newly evaluated.                                             2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
   Above 20MeV, the cross sections are the same as                2825 1451
ENDF/B-VII.1 (LA150).                                             2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
 MF  2: Resonance region                                          2825 1451
   MT 151: The resonance parameters are the same as               2825 1451
      in ENDF/B-VII.1, evaluated at ORNL. See the text below.     2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
 MF  3: Neutron cross sections                                    2825 1451
   MT   1: Total cross section, same as ENDF/B-VII.1.             2825 1451
   MT   4: Total inelastic scattering cross section               2825 1451
      sum of MT 51 - 91.                                          2825 1451
   MT  16: (n,2n) cross section                                   2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code, and adjusted                 2825 1451
      to avaialbe experimental data.                              2825 1451
   MT  22: (n,na) cross section                                   2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2825 1451
   MT  28: (n,np) cross section                                   2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code, and increased by 20%         2825 1451
      to better fit to experimental data.                         2825 1451
      Note that the activation data includes the (n,d) reaction.  2825 1451
   MT  51 - 91: (n,n') cross section                              2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2825 1451
      DWBA cross sections were given to                           2825 1451
      MT = 51, 52, 56, 62, and 70                                 2825 1451
   MT 102: (n,gamma) cross section                                2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code. The model parameters         2825 1451
      were adjusted to available experimental data and            2825 1451
      the evaluated MACS. However the new calculation does not    2825 1451
      change the MACS because the resonance boundary is 812 keV.  2825 1451
   MT 103: (n,p) cross section                                    2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code, and adjusted slightly        2825 1451
      to avaialbe experimental data near 3, 6, and 12 MeV.        2825 1451
   MT 104: (n,d) cross section                                    2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2825 1451
   MT 105: (n,t) cross section                                    2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2825 1451
   MT 107: (n,a) cross section                                    2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code, and adjusted slightly        2825 1451
      around 7 MeV for better fit to LANSCE alpha-production      2825 1451
      experiments (similar cross section as in ENDF/B-VII.1)      2825 1451
   MT 111: (n,2p) cross section                                   2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2825 1451
   MT 112: (n,pa) cross section                                   2825 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
 MF  4 Angular distributions of emitted neutrons                  2825 1451
   MT   2: elastic scattering                                     2825 1451
       0 - 800 keV:                                               2825 1451
          the P1, P2, and P3 were calculated                      2825 1451
          from the resonance parapeters,                          2825 1451
