***************************************************************** 2825 1451
Aug-2011, BNL, S. Hoblit                                          2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
The COMMARA-2.0 covariances were adopted for Ni-58 in the fast    2825 1451
neutron region. Here, like in the Cr and Fe materials, the        2825 1451
starting point was the ENDF/B-VI.8 covariances which resulted     2825 1451
from an evaluation by the highly experienced ORNL group. Then,    2825 1451
these data were subject to a dispersion analysis, leading to      2825 1451
certain modifications of uncertainties, while correlations were   2825 1451
left unchanged.                                                   2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
In the resonance region, a MF33/LB=5 section was added to the     2825 1451
covariances for elastic and total in the upper range of the       2825 1451
resonance region (6-775 keV) to account for the uncertainty in    2825 1451
the scattering radius R'. The uncertainty in R' was taken from    2825 1451
the Atlas of Neutron Resonances [1] and propagated to the elastic 2825 1451
cross sections using the energy bins of the AFCI COMMARA-2.0      2825 1451
processed files. To fully account for the uncertainty as given    2825 1451
in COMMARA-2.0, an additional 4% MF33/LB=1 section was added to   2825 1451
elastic from 248-775 keV and 8% LB1 section was added to capture  2825 1451
from 50-775 keV.                                                  2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
[1] S.F. Mughabghab,Atlas of Neutron Resonances, Elsevier, 2006   2825 1451
