Sheets), or were evaluated by Koning [Ko97].                      2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
  Only 2 measurements exist for neutron-induced emission spectra  2825 1451
above 20 MeV for 58Ni: the (n,x alpha) data by Haight et al       2825 1451
[Ha97], and (n,xp) data by Ullman et al [Ul83].  Some of the level2825 1451
density parameters were adjusted to give a good description of    2825 1451
these data.  Our starting point was the Gilbert-Cameron analysis  2825 1451
of Fu [Fu96], who studied the extreme sensitivity of calculated   2825 1451
cross sections on level densities for an IAEA CRP. Fu matched the 2825 1451
experimental D-0 value (14.4 keV) in 55Fe, and experimental       2825 1451
neutron, alpha, and proton emission data, by modifying the level  2825 1451
density a parameters. We modified Fu's 58Ni level density by 5% to2825 1451
a=6.5 to better describe Haight's data at 14 MeV. Above 14 MeV,   2825 1451
where (n,na) and (n,pa) become important, we increased the default2825 1451
level density a parameters in 54Fe and 54Mn by 7.5% to obtain an  2825 1451
improved agreement of the Haight data in the 40-50 MeV range (no  2825 1451
direct experimental information constrains these level densities).2825 1451
See Ref. [Ch97] for benchmark comparisons of the evaluation with  2825 1451
measured data.                                                    2825 1451
