                                                                  2825 1451
 ENDF/B-VI MOD 1 Evaluation, October 1989, D.C. Larson,           2825 1451
           C.M. Perey, D.M. Hetrick, and C.Y. Fu (ORNL)           2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
   THIS WORK EMPLOYED NUCLEAR MODEL CODES INCLUDING THE           2825 1451
DISTORTED WAVE BORN APPROXIMATION (DWBA) PROGRAM DWUCK (1)        2825 1451
AND THE HAUSER-FESHBACH CODE TNG (2,3,4).  THE TNG CODE PROVIDES  2825 1451
ENERGY AND ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF PARTICLES EMITTED IN THE      2825 1451
COMPOUND AND PRE-COMPOUND REACTIONS, ENSURES CONSISTENCY AMONG ALL2825 1451
REACTIONS, AND MAINTAINS ENERGY BALANCE. DETAILS PERTINENT TO THE 2825 1451
CONTENTS OF THIS EVALUATION AND EXTENSIVE COMPARISONS OF          2825 1451
CALCULATIONS WITH EXPERIMENTAL DATA CAN BE FOUND IN REFERENCE (5).2825 1451
                                                                  2825 1451
----- DESCRIPTION OF FILES                                        2825 1451
(MF-MT)                                                           2825 1451
  1-451 GENERAL INFORMATION, REFERENCES, AND DEFINITIONS.         2825 1451
  2-151 RESONANCE PARAMETERS ARE USED EXCLUSIVELY TO PROVIDE THE  2825 1451
        TOTAL, SCATTERING AND CAPTURE CROSS SECTIONS FROM 1.E-5 EV2825 1451
        TO 812 KEV, EXCEPT FOR CAPTURE FROM 450-812 KEV.  THE     2825 1451
        RESONANCE PARAMETERS ARE TAKEN FROM AN                    2825 1451
        EXTENSIVE RESONANCE PARAMETER ANALYSIS OF TRANSMISSION,   2825 1451
        SCATTERING AND CAPTURE DATA (6).  NEGATIVE ENERGY         2825 1451
        RESONANCES HAVE BEEN USED TO GIVE THE CORRECT THERMAL     2825 1451
        VALUES.  THE SCATTERING CROSS SECTION IS GIVEN COMPLETELY 2825 1451
        BY THE RESONANCE PARAMETERS FROM 1.E-5 TO 812 KEV, BUT FOR2825 1451
        THE CAPTURE CROSS SECTION, AVERAGE RESONANCE PARAMETERS   2825 1451
        USED FROM 450 TO 812 KEV.  THUS, THERE IS A BACKGROUND    2825 1451
        CONTRIBUTION IN 3/102 FROM 450 TO 812 KEV TO ACCOUNT FOR  2825 1451
        THE SMALL DIFFERENCE IN CAPTURE CROSS SECTION FROM THE    2825 1451
        AVERAGE RESONANCE PARAMETERS AND THE AVERAGED EXPERIMENTAL2825 1451
        DATA (6).  THE REICH-MOORE CODE SAMMY (7) WAS USED FOR THE2825 1451
        RESONANCE PARAMETER ANALYSIS.                             2825 1451
        THUS, THE THERMAL CROSS SECTIONS ARE GIVEN BY THE         2825 1451
        RESONANCE PARAMETERS AND HAVE VALUES: TOTAL 29.4 B,       2825 1451
        ELASTIC SCATTERING 24.8 B, AND CAPTURE 4.62 B.            2825 1451
        NOTE THAT THE FLAG HAS BEEN SET TO ALLOW USER CALCULATION 2825 1451
        OF THE ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS FROM THE R-M RESONANCE       2825 1451
        PARAMETERS, IF THE USER WANTS ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ON    2825 1451
        A FINER ENERGY GRID THAN GIVEN IN 4/2.                    2825 1451
  3-1   THE TOTAL CROSS SECTION WAS OBTAINED FROM .812 TO 20 MEV  2825 1451
        BY ANALYSIS OF THE SAME HIGH RESOLUTION MEASUREMENT       2825 1451
        USED FOR THE RESONANCE PARAMETER ANALYSIS IN 2/151. DATA  2825 1451
        WERE BINNED AND COMPARED WITH ENERGY AVERAGED DATA FROM   2825 1451
        ARGONNE (8) AND OTHER DATA FROM CSISRS, AND GOOD          2825 1451
        AGREEMENT WAS FOUND.                                      2825 1451
  3-2   ELASTIC SCATTERING CROSS SECTIONS WERE OBTAINED BY        2825 1451
        SUBTRACTING THE NONELASTIC FROM THE TOTAL                 2825 1451
  3-3   NONELASTIC CROSS SECTION; SUM OF 3-4, 3-16, 3-22,         2825 1451
        3-28, 3-102, 3-103, 3-104, AND 3-107.                     2825 1451
  3-4   TOTAL INELASTIC CROSS SECTION; SUM OF 3-51, 3-52, ..      2825 1451
        .., 3-58, AND 3-91                                        2825 1451
  3-16  (N,2N) CROSS SECTIONS WERE TAKEN FROM THE EVALUATION      2825 1451
        OF 58NI(N,2N)57NI CROSS SECTIONS BY PAVLIK AND            2825 1451
        WINKLER (9).  THESE CROSS SECTIONS WERE SLIGHTLY LARGER   2825 1451
        THAN THE TNG CALCULATIONS.  (SEE (N,NP) BELOW).           2825 1451
  3-22  (N,NA) + (N,AN) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE TNG 2825 1451
        CODE (2,3,4,5).  NO DATA AVAILABLE OTHER THAN A EMISSION. 2825 1451
  3-28  (N,NP) + (N,PN) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE TNG 2825 1451
        CODE (2,3,4,5) BUT MODIFIED ABOVE EINC OF 13.0 MEV TO FIT 2825 1451
        THE DATA OF PAVLIK ET AL. (10).  THE MODIFICATION OF THE  2825 1451
        TNG CALCULATION FOR (N,NP) CANCELED OUT THE DIFFERENCE    2825 1451
        BETWEEN THE TNG CALCULATION FOR (N,2N) AND THE ACTUAL     2825 1451
        (N,2N) USED (SEE ABOVE) SO THAT THE TNG CALCULATED        2825 1451
        NONELASTIC CROSS DID NOT CHANGE.                          2825 1451
  3-51 TO 3-58 INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING LEVELS; RESULTS ARE  2825 1451
        FROM TNG (2,3,4,5) WHICH INCLUDES DIRECT INTERACTION      2825 1451
        CROSS SECTIONS FROM DWUCK (1) CALCULATIONS. EXTENSIVE     2825 1451
        COMPARISONS WITH EXPERIMENTAL DATA USED IN THE EVALUATION 2825 1451
        PROCESS ARE SHOWN IN (5).                                 2825 1451
  3-91  INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING THE CONTINUUM (TNG          2825 1451
        CALCULATED).  GUIDANCE FROM (N,XN) EMISSION DATA (5).     2825 1451
  3-102 (N,G) CAPTURE CROSS SECTION IS PROVIDED ONLY BY RESONANCE 2825 1451
        PARAMETERS FROM 1.E-5 EV TO 450 KEV.  FROM 450 TO 812 KEV 2825 1451
        A SMALL BACKGROUND FILE IS GIVEN IN 3/102 TO COMBINE WITH 2825 1451
        THE 2/151 RESULTS.  TNG CALCULATIONS WERE NORMALIZED      2825 1451
        TO THE RESONANCE REGION RESULTS BETWEEN 100-812 KEV,      2825 1451
        AND USED FROM 812 KEV TO 20 MEV.                          2825 1451
  3-103 (N,P) CROSS SECTIONS UP TO 6 MEV WERE TAKEN FROM THE      2825 1451
        GLUCS (12) CALCULATION IN WHICH THIS REACTION WAS STUDIED 2825 1451
        SIMULTANEOUSLY WITH 12 OTHER DOSIMETRY REACTION CROSS     2825 1451
        SECTIONS (13).  FROM 6 TO 13 MEV A LINE WAS DRAWN         2825 1451
        THROUGH DATA (SEVERAL MEASURED DATA SETS DISAGREE AND A   2825 1451
        COMPROMISE WAS CHOSEN). ABOVE 13 MEV, TNG CALC. WERE USED 2825 1451
        WHICH COMPARED VERY WELL WITH RECENT MEASUREMENTS (5).    2825 1451
  3-104 (N,D) CROSS SECTION - TAKEN FROM ENDF/B-V (11) WHICH      2825 1451
        AGREED WELL WITH AVAILABLE DATA.                          2825 1451
  3-107 (N,A) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE               2825 1451
        TNG CODE (2,3,4,5) AND MODIFIED BETWEEN EINC FROM 7.0 TO  2825 1451
        13 MEV TO BETTER FIT THE RATIO DATA OF WATTECAMPS (14).   2825 1451
  4-2   ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY NEUTRONS FOR ELASTIC   2825 1451
        SCATTERING WERE REVIEWED AND ADOPTED FROM ENDF/B-V (11).  2825 1451
        IF DESIRED, ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS CAN BE CALCULATED BY    2825 1451
        THE USER ON A FINER ENERGY GRID FROM THE R-M RESONANCE    2825 1451
        PARAMETERS IN 2/151.                                      2825 1451
  6-16  (N,2N) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE  2825 1451
        NEUTRON AND 57NI RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELDS    2825 1451
        BASED ON TNG CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE GAMMA   2825 1451
        RAY; TNG CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR2825 1451
        EACH PRODUCT (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY FOR    2825 1451
        THE OUTGOING NEUTRON).  (N,XN) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY  2825 1451
        USED TO BENCHMARK THE TNG CALCULATIONS (5).               2825 1451
  6-22  (N,NA) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE  2825 1451
        NEUTRON, ALPHA, AND 54FE RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT   2825 1451
        YIELD BASED ON TNG CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE   2825 1451
        GAMMA RAY; CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN  2825 1451
        FOR EACH PRODUCT (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY    2825 1451
        FOR THE OUTGOING NEUTRON; ISOTROPY IS ASSUMED FOR THE     2825 1451
        ALPHA AND RESIDUAL). (N,XA) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY USED2825 1451
        TO BENCHMARK THE TNG CALCULATIONS (5).                    2825 1451
  6-28  (N,NP) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE  2825 1451
        NEUTRON, P, AND 57CO RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD 2825 1451
        BASED ON TNG CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE GAMMA   2825 1451
        RAY; CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR    2825 1451
        EACH PRODUCT (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY FOR    2825 1451
        THE OUTGOING NEUTRON).  (N,XP) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY  2825 1451
        USED TO BENCHMARK THE TNG CALCULATIONS (5).               2825 1451
  6-51 THROUGH 6-58 INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING LEVELS; EACH    2825 1451
        SECTION INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE NEUTRON   2825 1451
        AND 58NI RESIDUAL; ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR    2825 1451
        THE OUTGOING NEUTRON (LEGENDRE COEFFICIENTS COMPUTED      2825 1451
        BY DWUCK (1) AND TNG (2,3,4,5)).  EXTENSIVE COMPARISONS   2825 1451
        WITH ANGULAR DISTRIBUTION DATA ARE GIVEN IN (5).          2825 1451
  6-91  INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING THE CONTINUUM; INCLUDES     2825 1451
        SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE NEUTRON AND 58NI           2825 1451
        RESIDUAL AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD BASED ON TNG          2825 1451
        CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE GAMMA RAY; TNG       2825 1451
        CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN             2825 1451
        FOR EACH (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY FOR THE    2825 1451
        OUTGOING NEUTRON).  (N,XN) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY USED 2825 1451
        TO BENCHMARK THE TNG CALCULATIONS (5).                    2825 1451
  6-103 (N,P) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR P     2825 1451
        AND 58CO RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD BASED       2825 1451
        ON CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR GAMMA RAY;            2825 1451
        CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR EACH    2825 1451
        PRODUCT.  (N,XP) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY USED TO BENCH- 2825 1451
        MARK THE TNG CALCULATIONS (5).                            2825 1451
  6-107 (N,A) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR A     2825 1451
        AND 55FE RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD BASED       2825 1451
        ON CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR GAMMA RAY;            2825 1451
        CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR EACH    2825 1451
        PRODUCT. (N,XA) D-D EMISSION DATA HEAVILY USED TO BENCH-  2825 1451
        MARK THE TNG CALCULATIONS (5).                            2825 1451
 12-51 THROUGH 12-58 BRANCHING RATIOS FOR THE LEVELS, COMPILED    2825 1451
        BY HETRICK ET AL. (5), ARE GIVEN.                         2825 1451
 12-102 (N,G) CAPTURE; MULTIPLICITIES WERE TNG CALCULATED.        2825 1451
 14-51 THROUGH 14-58 AND 14-102 GAMMA RAY ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS   2825 1451
        ASSUMED TO BE ISOTROPIC.                                  2825 1451
